> Here is the definition of "zetro" in jbovlaste: x1 is 1x10**21 of
> x2 in dimension/aspect x3 (default is units)  
>     
> In 1 x 10**21, the multiplication "x" and the following "1" are
> treated as a letter "x" with a subscript "1".  

Yeah, that's a bug.  That's going to happen anywhere in the main
gismu or cmavo lists that there were places with "x" followed by a
number less than 6.  This is almost always place structure data, but
sometimes not.  We can really only fix them as we find them.

